The `objpool: ... used=280576 KiB` line is the high-water mark of the
reservation: 17.9M values were born over the warm read plus three timed reps,
and the arena handed out ~274 MiB once, not four times.

## Command — RSS at 1M, repeated reads in one process

`bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py` forces `force_tuples=True`, closes the cursor
between reads (so exactly one result is live at a time), and reports wall
ns/row, DB-API rows/s and `ru_maxrss` after every read. It repeats the read in
one process to show that storage is reused rather than appended.

The baseline image predates the job, so the same script is mounted read-only
into it; the change image can also mount it so both sides run identical code.

```
flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
  -e BENCH_GIT_REV=baseline -e FASTPOSTGRES_MATERIALIZE=1 \
  -v "$PWD/bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py:/src/bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py:ro" \
  fpq-baseline python3 /src/bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py 1000000 3'

flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
  -e BENCH_GIT_REV=object-reuse-off -e FASTPOSTGRES_MATERIALIZE=1 \
  -e FASTPOSTGRES_OBJ_ARENA=0 \
  -v "$PWD/bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py:/src/bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py:ro" \
  fpq-object-reuse python3 /src/bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py 1000000 3'

flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
  -e BENCH_GIT_REV=object-reuse-on \
  -v "$PWD/bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py:/src/bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py:ro" \
  fpq-object-reuse python3 /src/bench/jobs/object_reuse_rss.py 1000000 3'
```

