## ### AB

Same-image, pool off → on (the change isolated; one run each, `benchmarks.sh`
1M, eager path):

| metric | off | on | delta |
|---|---|---|---|
| DB-API eager rows/s | 3.77M | 4.89M | **+29.7%** |
| core interface rows/s | 3.84M | 4.86M | **+26.6%** |
| `read_rows` cycles/row | 676.4 | 418.7 | **−38.1%** |
| `stream()` rows/s (control: no values built) | 9.18M | 9.26M | +0.9% (noise) |
| 4 processes rows/s | 8.87M | 8.74M | −1.5% (noise) |

Same-image, pool off → on, `object_reuse_rss.py` 1M, best of 3:

| metric | off | on | delta |
|---|---|---|---|
| DB-API eager ns/row | 253.7 | 200.2 | **−21.1%** |
| DB-API eager rows/s | 3.94M | 4.99M | **+26.7%** |
| `read_rows` cycles/row | 694.0 | 467.1 | **−32.7%** |
| peak RSS | 379.0 MiB | 378.0 MiB | **−0.3% (flat)** |

Against the mandated baseline image (`fpq-baseline`, main@7e3d2e6; includes
whatever main has that this branch does not):

| metric | fpq-baseline | fpq-object-reuse | delta |
|---|---|---|---|
| DB-API eager rows/s | 3.98M | 4.89M | **+22.9%** |
| DB-API eager ns/row | 241.1 | 200.2 | **−17.0%** |
| `read_rows` cycles/row | 655.1 | 467.1 | **−28.7%** |
| peak RSS at 1M | 378.7 MiB | 378.0 MiB | **−0.2%** |

The RSS is the point: the old immortal arena was ~2x on object birth and leaked
~29 MiB per 100k-row read (several reads to ~3.9 GiB). This version keeps the
birth win and holds the footprint flat: 10 consecutive 1M-row reads, 49.3M
values born, arena `used` 202752 KiB and peak RSS 377.6 MiB, unchanged from the
first read. `fallbacks=0` at 1M; a read bigger than the 512 MiB cap falls back to
the normal constructors rather than growing past it.

## Tests

`flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g fpq-object-reuse tests.sh'`

```
### extension: make installcheck
ok
### client: unittest
Ran 61 tests in 1.515s
OK (skipped=1)
```

The new test is
`DbapiTest.test_shm_row_values_are_reusable_and_copyable`: it forces the row
frame, compares values, checks `copy.copy` / `copy.deepcopy` / pickle round
trips, releases the cells, and reads again to exercise reuse. All pre-existing
tests stay green.
